<a xmlns:tal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/tal"
   class="promo-cardlink"
   tal:define="card view/card_href;
               image view/image;
               actions view/actions"
   tal:attributes="href card"
   tal:omit-tag="not:card">
  <!--! The Promo's anatomy: ticket 17's class table, and the same markup
        `bundle-src/src/promo/PromoView.tsx` emits. One scope-wrapped
        stylesheet dresses both surfaces, so an element added here without a
        peer there is a bug in both.

        Commentary must use the `!` form above. Chameleon refuses an ASCII
        double hyphen anywhere inside a comment, including in prose, and an
        ordinary HTML comment would ship to every visitor besides.

        The indentation below is stripped by `PromoBlockView.__call__`; see its
        docstring for why an inter-element newline is not cosmetic here.

        THE CARD LINK IS A WRAPPER (ticket 17 rule 4), never a root whose tag
        changes to an anchor: `.promo`'s tag and class list are invariant
        across every state, which is the parity the whole design buys.
        `tal:omit-tag` drops this anchor whole when no card link survives the
        click rule. A stretched link overlay was rejected, because it would
        make the stylesheet load bearing for clickability, which is the one
        thing ticket 04 hands themes power over. -->
  <div tal:attributes="class view/root_class">
    <!--! Always `picture` + `img`, so `image_source()`'s scales or no scales
          branch is invisible to the sheet. `alt=""`: ticket 03 declared no alt
          field, so the picture is decorative. The title and description carry
          the meaning, and an alt invented from the title would be read twice.
          `width` and `height` are dropped by Chameleon when absent. -->
    <picture class="promo-image" tal:condition="image">
      <img alt=""
           decoding="async"
           loading="lazy"
           tal:attributes="src image/src;
                           width image/width;
                           height image/height" />
    </picture>
    <!--! Every element is conditional on its own content and no container is
          ever emitted empty (ticket 17 rule 3), so an empty promo is exactly
          one element. The editor's labelled skeleton lives outside the root
          and has no counterpart here: the public page says nothing about what
          an author typed and the renderers dropped. -->
    <div class="promo-copy" tal:condition="view/has_copy">
      <p class="promo-kicker"
         tal:condition="view/kicker"
         tal:content="view/kicker">Kicker</p>
      <!--! `h2`, not a configurable level: a promo that never enters the
            document outline is invisible to anyone navigating by heading, and
            a generic block cannot know its true depth. -->
      <h2 class="promo-title"
          tal:condition="view/title"
          tal:content="view/title">Title</h2>
      <p class="promo-description"
         tal:condition="view/description"
         tal:content="view/description">Description</p>
      <!--! No slot class: primary and secondary name appearance, not order,
            and DOM order gives `:first-child` to anyone who needs position.
            The variant is spelled `promo-cta-button` / `promo-cta-link` rather
            than as a `has` modifier, which is the shape that means plugin
            machinery: `align` has that upstream and the variant does not. -->
      <div class="promo-actions" tal:condition="actions">
        <a tal:repeat="action actions"
           tal:attributes="class action/css;
                           href action/href"
           tal:content="action/label">Label</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</a>
